1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,172
Who changed this page, and when?

2
00:00:03,172 --> 00:00:08,661
The Audit Trail module records changes made in the admin, so you can answer that question.

3
00:00:08,661 --> 00:00:13,120
In this video, you turn it on, make a change, and read the log it keeps.

4
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:21,047
With several people editing a site, questions come up:

5
00:00:21,047 --> 00:00:24,429
who published this page, and when did its title change?

6
00:00:24,429 --> 00:00:26,980
Without a record, the answer is a guess.

7
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:31,313
The Audit Trail module logs back-end changes as events.

8
00:00:31,313 --> 00:00:35,249
Each event has a category and a name, the user who caused it,

9
00:00:35,249 --> 00:00:37,070
and the time it happened.

10
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:43,436
The Contents module adds the Content category, with events such as Created, Saved,

11
00:00:43,436 --> 00:00:45,925
Published, Removed, and Restored.

12
00:00:45,925 --> 00:00:50,520
The Users Audit Trail feature adds User events, such as Logged in.

13
00:00:54,732 --> 00:00:56,772
Let's start in Tools, Features.

14
00:00:56,772 --> 00:00:58,370
Search for Audit Trail.

15
00:00:58,370 --> 00:01:03,112
It is listed in the Security category, with a short description of what it does.

16
00:01:03,568 --> 00:01:05,676
Click Enable on the Audit Trail row.

17
00:01:05,676 --> 00:01:08,988
A message confirms that the feature Audit Trail was enabled.

18
00:01:09,450 --> 00:01:13,726
With the feature enabled, the admin menu has two Audit Trail entries:

19
00:01:13,726 --> 00:01:18,400
one under Tools, for the log, and one under Settings, for its configuration.

20
00:01:22,615 --> 00:01:24,535
Open Settings, Audit Trail.

21
00:01:24,535 --> 00:01:28,781
The Events tab lists every event the module can record, each with a

22
00:01:28,781 --> 00:01:30,933
description and an Enabled box.

23
00:01:30,933 --> 00:01:33,725
The Content events are enabled by default.

24
00:01:34,179 --> 00:01:39,089
The Trimming tab sets the Retention period, which is 10 days unless you change it.

25
00:01:39,089 --> 00:01:41,879
A daily task deletes events older than that.

26
00:01:42,335 --> 00:01:46,316
On the Content tab, Allowed content types lists your content types.

27
00:01:46,316 --> 00:01:47,406
Check Article.

28
00:01:47,406 --> 00:01:51,115
Until you check a type, no content events are recorded for it.

29
00:01:51,571 --> 00:01:52,449
Click Save.

30
00:01:52,449 --> 00:01:55,601
A message confirms that the site settings were updated.

31
00:01:59,818 --> 00:02:01,260
Let's make a change.

32
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:05,918
Open Content, Content Items, search for Pruning, and click Edit on the Article

33
00:02:05,918 --> 00:02:09,078
Pruning workshop, which Jamie Chen created earlier.

34
00:02:09,534 --> 00:02:13,974
Change the Title to Pruning workshop for beginners, and click Publish.

35
00:02:14,441 --> 00:02:17,312
A message confirms that the Article was published.

36
00:02:17,312 --> 00:02:20,131
The module has recorded an event for this change.

37
00:02:24,345 --> 00:02:26,173
Open Tools, Audit Trail.

38
00:02:26,173 --> 00:02:29,281
Each row is one event, with the newest first.

39
00:02:29,281 --> 00:02:33,974
Its badges give the event name, the category, how long ago it happened,

40
00:02:33,974 --> 00:02:35,985
and the user who caused it.

41
00:02:36,466 --> 00:02:40,191
The text next to the badges names the version and the item.

42
00:02:40,191 --> 00:02:43,915
The version links to the item as it was then, and the title

43
00:02:43,915 --> 00:02:45,806
links to the item's editor.

44
00:02:46,282 --> 00:02:49,636
At the end of each row, View opens the item as it was

45
00:02:49,636 --> 00:02:52,819
at that version, and Details opens the full event.

46
00:02:52,819 --> 00:02:57,707
Published events whose version is no longer the latest, and Removed events, also

47
00:02:57,707 --> 00:02:59,242
get a Restore button.

48
00:02:59,711 --> 00:03:03,417
To narrow the list, use the Date and Category lists.

49
00:03:03,417 --> 00:03:06,612
The Sort list changes the order of the rows.

50
00:03:06,612 --> 00:03:10,511
Date offers ranges such as Last 24 hours and This week.

51
00:03:10,975 --> 00:03:15,184
Type a user name in the Search box to see one person's events.

52
00:03:15,184 --> 00:03:19,208
Searching for jamie keeps only the events that user caused.

53
00:03:19,208 --> 00:03:24,965
The Filters button opens a menu with Filter syntax, which lists the other search terms.

54
00:03:29,219 --> 00:03:31,380
Click Details on the first row.

55
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:35,118
The Audit Trail Event page opens with an Event Info table:

56
00:03:35,118 --> 00:03:38,799
the category, the event name, who triggered it, and when.

57
00:03:39,276 --> 00:03:44,497
Under it, Content Item Info shows the Content Item Id, the content type,

58
00:03:44,497 --> 00:03:49,116
the display text, the version, and any comment the editor left.

59
00:03:49,587 --> 00:03:53,140
A Diff tab on this page compares the item with the way the

60
00:03:53,140 --> 00:03:55,749
previous event for that item recorded it.

61
00:03:55,749 --> 00:03:59,357
A separate video shows how to compare and restore versions.

62
00:04:03,565 --> 00:04:07,865
To see the history of one item, open Content, Content Items.

63
00:04:07,865 --> 00:04:12,425
In the row of the Article, open Actions, and choose Audit Trail.

64
00:04:12,907 --> 00:04:15,756
The page lists only the events of that item.

65
00:04:15,756 --> 00:04:20,487
The Category list is replaced by an Events list, which filters by event name.

66
00:04:24,687 --> 00:04:27,042
Two permissions belong to the module:

67
00:04:27,042 --> 00:04:31,206
View audit trail, to read the log, and Manage audit trail settings, to

68
00:04:31,206 --> 00:04:32,849
change what is recorded.

69
00:04:32,849 --> 00:04:37,122
Opening Settings, Audit Trail also takes the Manage settings permission.

70
00:04:37,122 --> 00:04:39,587
The Administrator role has all of them.

71
00:04:40,337 --> 00:04:42,936
The module also provides a content part.

72
00:04:42,936 --> 00:04:46,440
Add it to a content type, and editors get a Comment box.

73
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:50,282
The comment is saved with the event, and it appears in the log

74
00:04:50,282 --> 00:04:52,147
and in the event's details.

75
00:04:52,897 --> 00:04:57,464
The Users Audit Trail feature records user events, such as Logged in.

76
00:04:57,464 --> 00:05:02,031
The Events tab also has an Allow client IP address box, and depending

77
00:05:02,031 --> 00:05:05,807
on your legislation, an IP address can be personal data.

78
00:05:05,807 --> 00:05:08,547
A separate video covers these settings.

79
00:05:10,547 --> 00:05:14,539
Audit Trail keeps a record of who changed what, and when.

80
00:05:14,539 --> 00:05:20,559
Enable it, choose the content types to record, and read the log under Tools, Audit Trail.

81
00:05:20,559 --> 00:05:22,207
Thanks for watching.

